Problem: There exist two complex numbers $c$, say $c_1$ and $c_2$, so that $-5 + 3i$, $8 - i$, and $c$ form the vertices of an equilateral triangle.  Find the product $c_1 c_2$.

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);

pair A, B;
pair[] C;

A = (2,2);
B = (5,1);
C[1] = rotate(60,A)*(B);
C[2] = rotate(60,B)*(A);

draw(A--C[1]--B--C[2]--cycle);
draw(A--B);

dot("$-5 + 3i$", A, W);
dot("$8 - i$", B, E);
dot("$c_1$", C[1], N);
dot("$c_2$", C[2], S);
[/asy]

Solve step by step. End with: The answer is [your answer].
